[h2]Build times[/h2]
Every build listed above has its craft time reduced to a quarter of vanilla:
[list]
[*]Most objects: [b]200 → 50[/b]
[*]Log Fence and Log Gate: [b]150 → 38[/b]
[*]Stick Fence: [b]100 → 25[/b]
[/list]

[h2]Notes[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Hinges are never discounted.[/b] A swinging door or gate needs a hinge at the top and bottom of each leaf, so singles keep 2 and double-width builds keep 4 - the vanilla counts.
[*][b]Blowtorch fuel is deliberately unchanged.[/b] It is a drainable tool rather than a consumed item, so welding still burns through fuel at the normal rate.
[*][b]Dirt, gravel and sand floors and wooden poles are not included.[/b] They already cost a single material in vanilla, and redefining them causes a script load error, so they are left alone.
[*][b]Safe to add to an existing save.[/b] Costs are read when you build, so already-placed constructions are unaffected.
[*][b]Safe to remove.[/b] Nothing is stored in your save; uninstalling simply restores vanilla costs.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Requires [b]Build 42[/b]. This mod redefines vanilla construction recipes, so it will conflict with any other mod that changes the cost or build time of the same walls, doors, windows, frames, stairs, floors, fences or gates. Whichever mod loads last wins.

[b]Mod ID:[/b] CheaperBuildingMultiplayerB42
